      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ALMIGHTY FEAR NZ (6) has been thereabouts over the longer trips here recently, and though is form over the mile is only modest, those runs have been in good company. He is likely to make a play for the front here, and if he leads, he will take plenty of pegging back. PESCO POLLO (9) brings the strongest recent form to the table after a determined 2-metre victory over this track and distance last start. He was a game fourth in G3 company over this trip before that, and he looks the one to beat. VALTINO (3) was an upset winner her 11 days ago, and he can make full use of this good draw. Stick with him. LEAF STRIDE NZ (11) had found his form two starts ago before breaking last time and finishing sixth, beaten only 7 metres. If he can stay focused, his best form gives him a chance. Each way value.",
